#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:12
msgid "Legal framework for e-invoicing in Saudi Arabia"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:14
msgid ""
"In Saudi Arabia, businesses must comply with `electronic invoicing "
"regulations <https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Introduction/"
"LawsAndRegulations/Documents/20230519_E-"
"Invoicing%20Implementation%20Resolution%20English.pdf>`_ established by the "
"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA) under the E-Invoicing Regulations "
"and their associated implementation resolutions. `The e-invoicing framework "
"<https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Introduction/Pages/What-is-e-"
"invoicing.aspx>`_ applies to taxpayers subject to VAT in the Kingdom and is "
"implemented in two phases. Phase 1 (Generation Phase) requires businesses to "
"generate and store electronic invoices and notes in a compliant electronic "
"format, including mandatory fields and QR codes. Phase 2 (Integration Phase) "
"introduces integration with ZATCA’s platform for invoice clearance and "
"reporting through APIs. Businesses must issue tax invoices for B2B "
"transactions and simplified tax invoices for B2C transactions in accordance "
"with ZATCA’s technical and procedural requirements. The framework also "
"requires the issuance of electronic credit and debit notes linked to the "
"original invoice, while ensuring invoice authenticity, integrity, and "
"traceability through structured XML formats and cryptographic controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:29
